<title>USA: Raytheon wins $460 mln Philippines contract.</title>
<headline>Raytheon wins $460 mln Philippines contract.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Engineers &amp; Constructors said on Wednesday it won a $460 million contract to build a 1200-megawatt, gas-fired power plant in the Philippines.</p>
<p>Raytheon, a unit of Raytheon Co, said it will complete the project in Ilijan, Batangas, by early 2002.</p>
<p>Ilijan is 75 miles south of Manila. The plant will be built for KEPCO Philippines, a unit of Korea Electric Power Co.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
